<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ERGO Q1 available profit down.</title>
<headline>ERGO Q1 available profit down.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Available profit			  17.4 vs 21.7</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  10.0 vs 11.1</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 3,281 vs 3,323</p>
<p>    Tonnes treated		    12,442,000 vs 12,836,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			   0.264 vs 0.259</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  38,057 vs 39,881</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     52,499 vs 56,198</p>
<p>Full name: East Rand Gold and Uranium Co Ltd, managed by Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - Ergo is on track to produce its forecast 12.3 tonnes of gold in 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
